.TH QORE-HUBSPOT-SCHEMAS 1 "September 2026" "Qore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qore-hubspot-schemas \- manage private HubSpot schema snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qore-hubspot-schemas
.RB [ --cache-dir " DIR"]
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicitly obtain and qualify current documents for the supported HubSpot v3 APIs.
All ten documents and all declared actions must qualify with the installed Qore
runtime before atomic activation. No live authenticated API operation is tested.
Packages contain no HubSpot schema documents and installation never downloads them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Download supported schemas from HubSpot's public API catalogue and activate them.
.TP
.B import DIR
Read ten NAME.swagger.json files from DIR, qualify and activate the snapshot.
.TP
.B status
Print the verified active snapshot's absolute directory.
.TP
.B rollback [DIGEST]
Requalify and activate the previous snapshot, or the specified snapshot digest.
.TP
.B run -- COMMAND [ARGS]
Run a command with the active immutable snapshot pinned in its environment.
Running applications retain their snapshot until restarted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QORE_HUBSPOT_SCHEMA_SNAPSHOT
Absolute immutable snapshot directory used by the HubSpot app.
.TP
.B QORE_TYPESCRIPT_MASTER_ACTION_SCRIPT
Set to /usr/share/qore-v8-app-catalogue/dist/index.js to enable this catalogue.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Default cache root; falls back to ~/.cache. Snapshots live under qore/hubspot.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. An update failure leaves the active snapshot unchanged.
The run command returns the child command's exit status.
.SH FILES
Snapshots and the active.json pointer belong to the application account, outside
package-owned directories. A crashed writer can leave .update-lock; confirm its
recorded PID has stopped before removing the stale lock. Snapshots are retained
until explicitly removed by the owner.
.SH NOTES
Run as the application account. Review HubSpot's Developer Terms at
https://legal.hubspot.com/hs-developer-terms before obtaining documents.
Endpoint availability is controlled by HubSpot. Unsupported changes fail closed.
.SH SEE ALSO
/usr/share/doc/qore-v8-app-catalogue/README.Debian
